{"id": "EUVD-2026-107246", "enisaUuid": "6a9196c3-8a83-3c3e-aefe-9e2fa221f87c", "description": "Trudesk through 1.2.11 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows administrators to delete arbitrary files by supplying encoded traversal sequences to DELETE /api/v1/backup/:backup. Attackers can also pass unvalidated file values to POST /api/v1/backup/restore to restore archives from, or extract to, paths outside the intended directories.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:39:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T15:48:28", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@leediay/multiple-vuln-trudesk-1211", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/controllers/backuprestore.js#L108-L118", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk/blob/v1.2.11/src/backup/restore.js#L69-L71", "https://github.com/polonel/trudesk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/trudesk-through-1.2.11-path-traversal-via-backup-delete-and-restore-api"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j4h3-fqpx-mh28", "CVE-2026-114399"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.51, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "eca825f5-bc24-30e9-9740-8f72e6c12e30", "product": {"name": "trudesk", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "51c1f94c-1268-3d71-a1de-8b8c05564d6d", "vendor": {"name": "polonel"}}], "isExploited": false}